From b739d846f59dc8fa3c3277526af4461239d38fd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarpediem <tarpediem@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:13:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Input: add ST FTS1BA90A touchscreen driver

Minimal driver for the fts1b FingerTip controller, protocol from the
Samsung vendor driver: power on (avdd, 1 ms, vdd, 5 ms), system reset,
wait for the ready event, chip ID / firmware / panel info reads, touch
type selection, event FIFO clear and scan on/off around input open and
close and system sleep. 16-byte events are read with 0x60/0x61.

The firmware in the IC is used as is: no flash, configuration or
calibration write is ever sent. The supplies are never switched off
(the 1.8 V rail is shared with the display on the Tab S7+).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig    |  11 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Makefile   |   1 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/stmfts1b.c | 567 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 579 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/stmfts1b.c

